<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Where the mid-ordinates are</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A region from \(x = {@a@}\) to \(x = {@b@}\) is split into \({@n@}\) strips of equal width \(h\).</p><p>Type k for the strip number, for example <code>2+3*k</code>. Use fractions such as <code>1/2</code>, not decimals.</p><p>(a) Find \(h\).</p><div>\(h =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Strip \(k\) runs from \(x = {@a@} + (k - 1)h\) to \(x = {@a@} + kh\). Write the \(x\)-coordinate of the middle of strip \(k\) in terms of \(k\).</p><div>\(x =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Which strip has its mid-ordinate at \(x = {@exd(X)@}\)?</p><div>Strip [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) \(h = \dfrac{ {@b@} - {@a@} }{ {@n@} } = {@hh@}\).</p><p>(b) The middle of a strip is halfway between its edges, so add the two edges and divide by \(2\):</p><p>\[x = \frac{\left({@a@} + {@hh@}(k - 1)\right) + \left({@a@} + {@hh@}k\right)}{2} = {@a@} + {@hh@}\left(k - \tfrac{1}{2}\right) = {@expand(tam)@}\]</p><p>Check with \(k = 1\): \(x = {@a@} + \tfrac{1}{2} \times {@hh@}\), halfway across the first strip.</p><p>(c) Solve \({@a@} + {@hh@}\left(k - \tfrac{1}{2}\right) = {@exd(X)@}\): \(k - \tfrac{1}{2} = {@exd(X-a)@} \div {@hh@} = {@exd(kk0-1/2)@}\), so \(k = {@kk0@}\). Strip \({@kk0@}\) runs from \(x = {@a+(kk0-1)*hh@}\) to \(x = {@a+kk0*hh@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* exd: shortest exact decimal display of a terminating value (up to 3 d.p.) */
exd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else dispdp(float(v),3);
validate_k(ex) := if every(lambda([v], member(v, [k])), listofvars(ex)) then "" else "Write your answer in terms of k only.";
/* Design: positions of the mid-ordinates. Entries [a, b, n, k0]; h is a whole number on every entry. The strip index is k here (STACK reads i as the square root of -1). Source: original. */
L: [[2,10,4,3],[1,16,5,2],[5,25,4,4],[3,27,6,5],[10,40,5,2],[4,10,3,2],[20,80,6,4],[1,13,4,3],[6,30,8,6],[2,32,5,4]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
a: L[ix][1]; b: L[ix][2]; n: L[ix][3]; kk0: L[ix][4];
hh: (b-a)/n;
X: a+(kk0-1/2)*hh;
tam: a+(k-1/2)*hh;
/* diagnostics */
dR: a+k*hh; dL: a+(k-1)*hh; dH: a+k*hh/2; dA: (k-1/2)*hh; dP: a+(k+1/2)*hh;]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
